LLVM PolyBench floating-path source audit, 2026-09-16.
Scope: the following 29 unchanged LLVM SingleSource C programs, not the separate E8 adapter.
Upstream commit: 2919e55176a572ee085cb46b291c47b7092c363e.
This is a source/command audit, not a new GCC/Clang or EvoCC execution result.
The original Clang-19 ARM64 control reports PASS for each in the existing run
.evidence/ladder/llvm-test-suite/20260915T152557Z/lit-baseline.json.
That run's compile-commands.json and the disposition ledger bind the complete original options.
Raw outcomes and the 1735-program LLVM denominator are not rewritten.

Shared source: SingleSource/Benchmarks/Polybench/utilities/polybench.h
SHA256: 06a482eac0a930592356a52b3aa844856cfdc3bea00606f47d1b09e90d5df9d4
At line 827 print_element takes double; print_array calls it for each result.
Every selected command defines POLYBENCH_DUMP_ARRAYS, so this output is enabled.
For the 12 commands with -DFMA_DISABLED=1 the secondary check is disabled;
this does not eliminate their floating-array kernels or double output.
Of the 17 other programs, 16 invoke check_FP: double temporaries, fabs and comparison.
fdtd-2d defines but does not call check_FP; its executed floating stencil and
double output, not that unused check, establish its floating requirement.
In particular nussinov and floyd-warshall use integer algorithm data, but that
actual original validation/output still executes floating conversions and values.
The separate E8 nussinov smoke has different upstream support code and remains separate.
No FP obligation is inferred merely from an unused declaration or diagnostic code.

